<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila, IMF agree on 21.5 pct M3 growth rate.</title>
<headline>Manila, IMF agree on 21.5 pct M3 growth rate.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) set a monetary programme calling for an average M3 growth rate of 21.5 percent this year, a joint statement said.</p>
<p>In 1996, the programme called for a maximum M3 growth of 25.8 percent but Philippine Central Bank officials said the growth rate was lower.</p>
<p>M3 is the broadest measure of liquidity.</p>
</text>
